  "planning_notes": [
    "Buttons D2/D3/D4 represent arrival to floors 1..3; digital_input initial is false (button not pressed). Active polarity (active_high/pullup) is not specified in the provided wiring; default catalog polarity is assumed.",
    "A0 is used as a raw analog_input; conversion from ADC to load percent and overload threshold are model responsibilities.",
    "TM1637 is used via tm1637_number on CLK=D7 and DIO=D5. The display content (floor vs load percent) and its switching cadence are handled in SysML; this interface only provides a single numeric channel.",
    "Buzzer D6 uses tone_output. Alarm activation policy and tone frequency/duration are model responsibilities; this interface provides only the tone command.",
    "Serial: original requirement states that when a floor-change button triggers, the system simulates movement delay and outputs 'movement complete'. Exact output text/protocol is not specified; assumption: report includes one structured numeric value (movement duration in ms) on a dedicated trigger gate.",
    "Additional overload state reporting cadence and exact fields are not specified; assumption: a separate report group exists for overload events/states with load percent, floor, and overload boolean."
  ],
